      "phase": "token",
      "summary": "Client mints and signs a JWT bearer assertion.",
      "detail": "There is no authorization request, redirect, or consent screen. The client (a trusted issuer for its users) signs a short-lived assertion with its own private key: 'iss' identifies the issuer, 'sub' is the user the token will be scoped to, 'aud' is the token endpoint, and a fresh 'jti' plus a short 'exp' make it one-time and time-boxed. Only the assertion's public key is registered with the authorization server; the private key never leaves the client.",
      "outcome": "ok",
      "refs": [],
